WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Moderator: What do you need from your customer success tools?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Tom Okafor: I'm VP of customer success. I need to know three things: which renewals are at risk, why, and what we're doing about it. I mostly get a score and a red dot.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Tom Okafor: I can't defend a number I can't explain. In board meetings someone asks why an account is red and I can't answer without calling my ops manager. I don't trust the health score enough to act on it.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Moderator: How do you find out about problems today?

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Tom Okafor: Usually late. A CSM tells me in our weekly meeting, or the customer's executive calls me. The early warning in the product doesn't reach me, there's too much noise.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:59.000
Tom Okafor: My team spends too much time preparing numbers. Reporting is manual, and it's out of date by the time I see it.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Tom Okafor: What I'd love is a portfolio view: renewals by quarter, risk by reason, and what's changed this week. With a click to the account behind it.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.000
Moderator: What matters most about the team's workflow?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:59.000
Tom Okafor: Handoffs. When support and success don't share context, customers feel it. We've lost renewals over a dropped escalation.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Tom Okafor: If I could show the board that every risk has an owner and a plan, that would change the conversation.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:46.000
Tom Okafor: Honestly the customer timeline is the best part of the product. My CSMs say it saves them an hour a day. I wish the rest felt like that.

